 JSON in, JSON out. Routes are listed in `README.md`.

+## Authentication
+
+Send `Authorization: Bearer <key>` with every request. The data file's
+`apiKeys` array holds records with `key`, `name`, and `role`. Existing data
+without keys needs an `apiKeys` entry before it can serve authenticated
+requests. For local demos, start with a copy of `data/seed.json` as
+`LARDER_DATA`. Its keys are `seed-viewer`, `seed-cook`, and `seed-manager`.
+
+- `viewer` can use GET routes except `/audit`.
+- `cook` has viewer access and can use `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures`, and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager` can use every route.
+
+Missing or invalid credentials return 401 (`unauthorized`). A key with
+insufficient permissions returns 403 (`forbidden`).
+
+## Routes
+
+See the [full route list](../README.md#routes) for kitchen operations.
+
+`GET /audit` returns a JSON array for managers, newest entries first.
+Each successful request that changes data adds an entry with `at` (UTC
+timestamp), `keyName`, `method`, `path` (without query parameters), and
+`status` (HTTP status code).
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
